WEBVTT

1
00:00.001 --> 00:11.180
First, the analytics notice: No thanks.

2
00:11.180 --> 00:18.193
A public sample World that opens without signing up: a read-only sample compiled from Apple's public SEC filings.

3
00:18.193 --> 00:24.651
Prepared retrieval results from this artifact. Free-form AI queries are not running in this public demo.

4
00:24.651 --> 00:28.651
Pick one of the prepared questions.

5
00:28.651 --> 00:37.044
The answer is a source passage chosen by retrieval. Under it, the page says it is a quotation, not an independently checked conclusion.

6
00:37.044 --> 00:42.414
Each excerpt names its source file and page. Choosing a row opens that page.

7
00:42.414 --> 00:47.003
The source page opens, with the region the excerpt came from marked on it.

8
00:47.003 --> 00:53.159
The source version is pinned by its content hash, and each piece of evidence has a permanent link.

9
00:53.159 --> 00:58.550
The evidence inspector opens one object beside the source region that supports it.

10
00:58.550 --> 01:05.890
Next steps through the source regions behind this object, one at a time.

11
01:05.890 --> 01:12.304
Change sets the World built from the annual filing beside the same World after later filings arrived.

12
01:12.304 --> 01:16.314
Each filing that arrived is shown with its source page.

13
01:16.314 --> 01:24.756
The comparison runs object by object and counts rebuilt and unchanged identities separately. It is a comparison recorded in this sample.

14
01:24.756 --> 01:29.726
A page with no region is marked as such, and nothing in this World stands on it.

15
01:29.726 --> 01:35.235
The Evidence page shows every region a World read from one page.

16
01:35.235 --> 01:40.265
Each region carries a locator: its page, its box coordinates and the source hash.

17
01:40.265 --> 01:46.074
Open this region in Explore takes the same region back into Explore.

18
01:46.074 --> 01:53.771
We arrange intake for your own sources with you.
